</Fragment>
<main id="main">

<!-- LABEL -->
<div style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:40px 40px 0"><span style="font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Portfolio</span></div>
<!-- HERO -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:70px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px 96px;align-items:center"><div style="flex:1 1 320px;max-width:480px;min-width:0"><img decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" src="images/elise-portrait.webp" alt="Portrait of Elise L’Hopitault." style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 30%;border-radius:4px"></div><div style="flex:1 1 420px;min-width:0;max-width:760px"><h1 style="margin:0;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:50px;letter-spacing:.03em;line-height:1.15">About me</h1><p style="margin:12px 0 28px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:18px;letter-spacing:.04em;color:#8B5A61">Web developer turned product designer</p><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">I have always been creative. I drew and painted as a child, and I still paint when I find the time. I started a degree in 3D design for video games and animated films, then trained as a web developer.</p><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">Product design brought both together: the creativity I started with, in something concrete that people actually use. It suits me better.</p><p style="margin:0 0 0px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">AI is part of my daily work now. Some people are wary of it, I am not: I use these tools to work faster and more efficiently, as collaborators rather than replacements. At work I have access to several AI assistants, and I pick the right one for the task. The thinking, the decisions and the quality of what I deliver stay mine.</p></div></div></div>
<!-- DESIGN + DEV -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:130px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;color:#641822">Between design and development</h2><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:40px 96px"><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:760px;min-width:0"><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">At ENGIE, I work on GPC 2.0, an executive reporting product built in Power BI. Many of the people involved were not familiar with Power BI, so the ideas and needs they brought did not always fit what the tool can do. Some components, for example, simply cannot be built in it.</p><p style="margin:0 0 0px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">That is where I step in. I help adapt those needs to Power BI: I explain to the designers what the tool allows, and to the developers what the design is meant to achieve, then we find a compromise or another way to reach the same goal. Having worked in development myself, I speak both languages.</p></div><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:560px;min-width:0;border-left:2px solid #641822;padding-left:28px"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:10px">How I work</div><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">I am a perfectionist, but an efficient one. When I am asked for a mock-up, I prioritize the information and the real need, and I structure the work so it stays readable.</p><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:10px">Beyond the main project</div><p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">I take on smaller dashboard redesigns on my own, to build autonomy and grow toward project management.</p></div></div></div>
<!-- TOOLS -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:130px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;color:#641822">Tools I work with</h2><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:40px 96px"><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:660px;min-width:0;"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:16px">Design and product</div><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px"><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Figma</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Power BI</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Jira</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Claude</span></div><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:10px"><span style="border:1.5px solid #B9858D;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Figma Make</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #B9858D;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Notion</span></div></div><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:660px;min-width:0;border-left:2px solid #641822;padding-left:28px"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:16px">Development</div><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px"><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">HTML / CSS</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">JavaScript</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">React</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">Node.js</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">MongoDB</span><span style="border:1.5px solid #641822;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.3">GitHub</span></div></div></div></div>
<!-- PATH -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:130px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;color:#641822">My path</h2><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:48px 96px"><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:660px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:10px">Experience</div><div style="border-top:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:6px">Oct 2025 → 2027</div><div style="font-weight:600;font-size:17px">Product Designer, work-study</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px">ENGIE, La Défense</div></div><div style="padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:6px">Sept 2024 → Sept 2025</div><div style="font-weight:600;font-size:17px">Web Developer, work-study</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px">ENGIE, La Défense</div></div></div></div><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:660px;min-width:0"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:10px">Education</div><div style="border-top:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:6px">2025 → 2027</div><div style="font-weight:600;font-size:17px">Product Design, BA level</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px">OpenClassrooms, work-study</div></div><div style="padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:6px">2024 → 2025</div><div style="font-weight:600;font-size:17px">Web Development, two-year degree</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px">OpenClassrooms, work-study</div></div><div style="padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #D9D2C7"><div style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#8B5A61;margin-bottom:6px">2020 → 2022</div><div style="font-weight:600;font-size:17px">Art and Design</div><div style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;margin-top:2px">École Brassart: applied arts, first year of 3D animation and VFX</div></div></div></div></div></div>
<!-- CERAMICS -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:130px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;color:#641822">Made by hand</h2><div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:40px 72px;align-items:flex-start"><div style="flex:1 1 420px;max-width:640px;min-width:0"><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">Before design, there was clay. At three or four years old, I already knew I wanted to become a potter. Life took me elsewhere, but the need to make things with my hands never left: I have always drawn, painted and create with my hands.</p><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">This September, I finally started wheel-throwing classes in a studio. I am a beginner, working on small pieces, and it nourishes me.</p><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">A piece takes weeks, sometimes months: first throwing the shape, then trimming it, then glazing. Each stage asks for patience, and for picturing the final piece long before it exists.</p><p style="margin:0 0 0px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">One of my pieces came off the wheel while I was trimming it. My first reflex would have been to throw it away. Instead, I reshaped it, gave it another chance and carried on. It now has a small scar, and with it a story before it is even finished. That makes it all the more endearing to me, and I cannot wait to see it glazed.</p></div><div style="flex:1 1 520px;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:20px"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="images/ceramics-pieces.webp" alt="Three unglazed pieces made on the wheel: a tall cup and two bowls." style="display:block;border-radius:4px;aspect-ratio:4/5;width:100%;flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 60%"><img decoding="async" loading="lazy" src="images/ceramics-bowl.webp" alt="A trimmed bowl in raw clay, ready for glazing, next to a taller cup." style="display:block;border-radius:4px;aspect-ratio:4/5;width:100%;flex:1 1 220px;min-width:0;object-fit:cover;object-position:42% center"><div style="background:#E6E3DB;border-radius:4px;aspect-ratio:4/5;width:100%;display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;gap:8px;color:#6B5A53;text-align:center;padding:16px;box-sizing:border-box;flex:1 1 220px;"><span style="font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase">Coming soon</span><span style="font-size:14px;max-width:300px">Oil painting.</span></div></div></div></div>
<!-- QUOTE -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:120px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><blockquote style="margin:0;padding:8px 0 8px 32px;border-left:3px solid #641822;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:600;font-size:30px;line-height:1.35;max-width:1000px">Care about the details, without chasing a perfection that does not exist.</blockquote></div>
<!-- LOOKING -->
<div style="width:100%;max-width:1427px;margin:130px auto 0;padding:0 32px 0px;box-sizing:border-box"><h2 style="margin:0 0 34px;font-family:'Roboto Mono',monospace;font-weight:700;font-size:32px;line-height:1.2;color:#641822">Where I am heading</h2><div style="max-width:760px"><p style="margin:0 0 20px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">I am looking to join a product team where I can keep bridging design and development, and take on more ownership of projects.</p><p style="margin:0 0 28px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6">Available from April 2027. Based in Tours, open to Paris and to relocation abroad.</p><a href="resume/Elise-LHopitault-CV-Product-Designer-EN.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;background:#641822;color:#F5F3EE;text-decoration:none;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;padding:14px 22px;border-radius:6px;min-height:44px;box-sizing:border-box">View my resume<svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="#F5F3EE" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 8h12M9 3l5 5-5 5"></path></svg></a></div></div>
</main>
<!-- CONNECT -->
</Layout>
